delivery plugin: third-party methods

The delivery plugin ports methods (the doctrine, not the code) from the projects below.
Each is under the MIT License; their copyright lines are reproduced here. The places that
use each method name it and point to this file.

amplifier-skill-taste (https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-skill-taste)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Taste × Elegance contributors. MIT License.
  Used in: skills/brief (the owner's lens in at most three questions, what must survive,
  gates first), templates/brief.md.

amplifier-skill-sizzle (https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-skill-sizzle)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Sizzle contributors. MIT License.
  Used in: skills/brief (one proposition), skills/prd (the one-breath test, cuts as proposed
  non-goals, the storyboard approved before any spend and reopened by change),
  skills/roadmap (the storyboard gate), templates/storyboard.md.

amplifier-skill-market-fit (https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-skill-market-fit)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Market Fit contributors. MIT License.
  Used in: skills/prd and templates/prioritization.md (the leftover test, after its
  "leftover stone").

amplifier-smart-tool-decisioncraft (https://github.com/michaeljabbour/amplifier-smart-tool-decisioncraft)
  Copyright (c) 2026 Decisioncraft contributors. MIT License.
  Used in: scripts/operator.js record --over and lib/operator-records.js (a decision keeps
  the options turned down, after its options' status and status_reason), skills/decision.

Market Fit (above) also: its choice log ("the choice, the option they turned down, and their
  reason"), in record --over.

